{"id":3929,"date":"2021-10-25T14:00:03","date_gmt":"2021-10-25T21:00:03","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=3929"},"modified":"2025-10-23T13:21:52","modified_gmt":"2025-10-23T20:21:52","slug":"1-5-conditionals-junior-cde-blockly","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/1-5-conditionals-junior-cde-blockly\/","title":{"rendered":"1.5: Conditionals"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22134381f88\" name=\"6a22134381f88\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>We've Moved!<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text css=&#8221;.vc_custom_1761250910202{padding-top: 20px !important;padding-right: 20px !important;padding-bottom: 20px !important;padding-left: 20px !important;background-color: #ffdddd !important;border-radius: 3px !important;}&#8221;]<\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-11766\" src=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/06\/icon_warning-150x150-2-84x85.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"81\" height=\"82\" \/><\/p>\n<p data-pm-slice=\"1 1 []\"><strong>We\u2019ve moved to our new lesson portal: <a href=\"http:\/\/learn.robolink.com\">Robolink Learn<\/a>! Lessons here will remain available until the end of June 2026. This version of Basecamp will no longer be updated and uses outdated references to Blockly for Robolink. You can access the previous version of <a href=\"https:\/\/codrone.robolink.com\/edu\/blockly-archive\/\">Blockly here<\/a>.<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221343820bb\" name=\"6a221343820bb\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>What are Conditionals?<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><strong>Conditionals<\/strong> are statements that help programs make decisions depending on if the statement is true or false. In programming, conditionals include if, else if, and else statements. <\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;7256&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<p class=\"p1\">You actually use conditionals to make decisions in your own life! This is how you might use if statements, which usually look like &#8220;if _____, then _____.&#8221;:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"li1\"><strong>If<\/strong> it is raining, I will take my umbrella. <strong>Else<\/strong>, I will stay inside.<\/li>\n<li class=\"li1\"><strong>If<\/strong> it is sunny, I will play outside. <strong>Else<\/strong>, I will stay inside.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>The else statement can be helpful if you want your program to do something different when the if statement is false.<\/p>\n<p>In summary, conditional statements are the program&#8217;s way of making decisions based on input.[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213438214f\" name=\"6a2213438214f\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>If Statements<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The <strong>if statement<\/strong> block is in the light purple &#8220;Logic&#8221; menu and has two parts.<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;5507&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;5509&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The first part is the notch next to the &#8220;if&#8221;, and this is where you would put the condition. This is the &#8220;if _____&#8221; part of an if statement. What you put in this space can only be true or false. Some examples include:\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If the up button is pressed\u00a0<\/span><\/li>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If 2 is even\u00a0<\/span><\/li>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If the battery percentage is less than 25\u00a0<\/span><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The next part is the space beneath the &#8220;if _____&#8221; part of the if statement. This is where you include the &#8220;then _____&#8221; part of the statement. You can do this by finding the block you need in the menus, and then dragging and dropping it into that space so the blocks connect.\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">This is how an if statement works once you run it:\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Your program will check the if statement. <\/span>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If the condition is true, it will run the code within the if statement, and once that&#8217;s finished, your program will run the code after the if statement. <\/span><\/li>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If the condition is false, your program will skip the if statement and run the code after the if statement.<\/span><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221343821ad\" name=\"6a221343821ad\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Program an If Statement<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">You have everything you need to program your first if statement! Program your drone to take off and then hover for five seconds if 5 is greater than 10.<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;5510&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">You can find an equation box in the light purple &#8220;Logic&#8221; menu, and you can select inequality signs from the drop-down menu.\u00a0<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;5511&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><strong>Number<\/strong> blocks are in the gray &#8220;Math&#8221; menu. Don\u2019t forget to have it land!\u00a0<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;5512&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Next, use the same program but switch the greater than sign to a less than sign&#8230;just to see what happens!<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;5513&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213438222c\" name=\"6a2213438222c\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 5<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Else Statements<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">There might be times when you want your program to do one thing if the condition is true and a completely different thing if the condition is false. In those cases, you would use an else statement, which is part of the <strong>if statement<\/strong> block. Just click on the blue gear icon and then drag and connect the <strong>else <\/strong>block to the <strong>if statement<\/strong> block.\u00a0<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;5514&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;5515&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Else statements are usually written as &#8220;If _____, then ______. Else, _____.&#8221;<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The first part of the <strong>else statement<\/strong> block looks just like an if statement! There&#8217;s a space for your condition and another space for what happens when your condition is true. The second part of the else statement is for the &#8220;Else, _____&#8221; part of your else statement. To include what action should be taken if the program is false, find the block you need in the menus, and then drag and drop it into the space underneath the <strong>else<\/strong> so the blocks connect.\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">This is how an else statement works once you run it:\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Your program will check the &#8220;if&#8221; part of the statement. <\/span>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If the condition is true, it will run the code within the if statement, and once that&#8217;s finished, your program will run the code after the if statement. <\/span><\/li>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If the condition is false, your program will run the code within the else statement, and once that&#8217;s finished, your program will run the code after the else statement.<\/span><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22134382277\" name=\"6a22134382277\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 6<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Program an Else Statement<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Program your drone to take off. Next, if &#8220;pi&#8221;, which is in the gray &#8220;Math&#8221; menu under its symbol, is greater than 3 it will fly forward. Else, it will fly backward.<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;13372&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213438235d\" name=\"6a2213438235d\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 7<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Else If Statement<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Sometimes you might want to have more than two options when making a decision. If that is the case, you can use an else if statement between your if and else statements. To use an else if statement, click on the blue gear icon in the <strong>if statement<\/strong> block from the light purple &#8220;Logic&#8221; menu, and then drag the <strong>else if<\/strong> block to the <strong>if<\/strong> block. You\u2019ll see that, just like an <strong>if statement<\/strong> block, there is a notch for your conditional and then a space for what will happen if the condition is true.\u00a0<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;5517&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;5518&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">This is how an else if statement works once you run it:\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Your program will check the &#8220;if&#8221; part of the statement. <\/span>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If the condition is true, it will run the code within the if statement, and once that&#8217;s finished, your program will run the code after the if statement. <\/span><\/li>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If the condition is false, your program will move on to the else if statement. If the condition is true, it will run the code within the else if statement, and once that\u2019s finished, your program will run the code after the else if statement. <\/span><\/li>\n<li>If the condition is false, your program will run the code within the else statement, and once that&#8217;s finished, your program will run the code after the else statement.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">You can have as many else if statements as you want in a program! Just remember there should always be a beginning if statement.<\/span>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22134382411\" name=\"6a22134382411\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 8<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Program an Else If Statement<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Program your drone so that if 7 is an even number, your CoDrone EDU will turn left. Else if 8 is an even number, your CoDrone EDU will fly backward for 1 second. Else, your CoDrone EDU will hover for 2 seconds.\u00a0<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;7626&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">After testing this version out, use the drop-down menus to change your options. <em>What happens when you set both numbers to odd, or when 7 is even and 8 is odd?<\/em><\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;7625&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;7624&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22134382503\" name=\"6a22134382503\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 9<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Challenges<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<strong>Challenge: Random Destination<\/strong><\/p>\n<div>\n<div>In this challenge, program your CoDrone EDU to fly to different locations depending on a randomly generated number. The <strong>random number generator<\/strong> block can be found in the &#8220;Math&#8221; menu.<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;10144&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<div>\n<div>Here are some tips to help you build out your program.<\/div>\n<ul>\n<li>Takeoff<\/li>\n<li>Generate a random integer from 1 to 50 and save it to a variable<\/li>\n<li>If the number is less than 15, go forward<\/li>\n<li>Else if the number is less than 30, go left<\/li>\n<li>Else if the number is less than 45, go backward.<\/li>\n<li>Land<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<div>\n<div><strong>Challenge: CoDrone EDU Calculator<\/strong><\/div>\n<div><\/div>\n<div>Get your CoDrone EDU to do your math for you! Program your CoDrone EDU to fly in different patterns based on if the mathematical equations you answer are true or false.<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;7715&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<div>\n<div><strong>Hint:<\/strong> There are blocks that are more complex than the <strong>number<\/strong> block. If you want to use these in an equation, drag the light purple <strong>equation<\/strong> block to your workspace and then drag the block you need into one of those blank spaces.<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;5519&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22134382567\" name=\"6a22134382567\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 10<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Lesson Complete<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]In this lesson, you learned all about conditionals and how they can be used to help your CoDrone EDU make decisions! You can use these conditional statements to program the CoDrone EDU to do different things depending on the statements you include.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;7547&#8243; img_size=&#8221;750&#215;670&#8243; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 11 We've Moved! [vc_column_text css=\".vc_custom_1761250910202{padding-top: 20px !important;padding-right: 20px !important;padding-bottom: 20px !important;padding-left: 20px !important;background-color: #ffdddd !important;border-radius: 3px !important;}\"] We\u2019ve moved to our new lesson portal: Robolink Learn! Lessons here&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/1-5-conditionals-junior-cde-blockly\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":4741,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":false,"_lesson_complexity":"","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":3877,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[1814,1760,1817,1777,1793,626,1533,1438,853,144,171,63],"lesson-tag":[2135,2108,4328,14401,2119,2123,2122],"class_list":["post-3929","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-beginner","lesson-tag-blockly","lesson-tag-cde","lesson-tag-cdej","lesson-tag-conditionals","lesson-tag-fundamentals","lesson-tag-programming","module-beginner","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/3929","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/lesson"}],"version-history":[{"count":44,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/3929\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":13618,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/3929\/revisions\/13618"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/4741"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=3929"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"lesson-category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-category?post=3929"},{"taxonomy":"lesson-tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-tag?post=3929"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}